# Change Log

## [0.1.0] - 2026-08-15

Add original read-only Tar File System from [related project](https://github.com/JBlaschke/CUG-Paper/blob/main/figures/scripts/analysis/src/io.jl)

## [0.2.0] - 2026-08-15

Full Read-Write Mode enabled

### Added

1. Ability to write to archive in memory (and save as a compressed tar file)
2. Added basic round-trip test

### Changed

1. The tar stream goes straight into the gzip compressor — the full
   uncompressed intermediate IOBuffer is gone.
2. Writing out no longer materializes/caches source-backed files; they stream
   from tarball_io via Tar.read_data.

### Fixed

1. `write_tarball_gz` is atomic (temp file + same-dir rename): a failure
   mid-write can no longer truncate the target, which makes `from = path`
   read-modify-write actually safe.
2. Entries >= 8 GiB error out (USTAR's 11-octal-digit size field) instead of
   silently emitting a malformed header.
3. `writefile` validates paths (relative, no ".."/empty segments/NUL), which
   also closes a joinpath() escape in the Tar.create variant.
